b-6409-555d-a3b2-ddc246163bdf","export":true,"mirror_uv":false,"isOpen":false,"locked":false,"visibility":false,"autouv":0,"rotation":[0,0,0],"children":["9706e29b-531b-5edd-9a5a-90bdfef0b4b2","5fac454e-4828-55cc-877d-8fae65640e60","a2c3dee1-2784-5797-be35-34a4fe8db520","f28eb8f1-66c0-570f-bb73-808a012dc223"]},{"name":"ruined","origin":[0.0,0.0,0.0],"color":0,"uuid":"c589df4f-4b87-541e-8045-388c69647265","export":true,"mirror_uv":false,"isOpen":false,"locked":false,"visibility":false,"autouv":0,"rotation":[0,0,0],"children":["e38827e7-82c3-5237-a3de-a12e177511d4","3b40852c-717d-5a31-bb64-07e83729cac7","11466fd5-2433-5b49-b57a-b821946b4d79","c85c68ad-354f-5f2e-9a71-b936397ad6dc","a14cab97-496d-5b29-8ad0-17af946079f7","55c0a41e-18d7-58bf-8005-fbf965b9abe3","02a50c7a-a4af-573b-90c5-92609f4aa52b","84c2d796-2cde-5183-a11f-b745fdfc6a01","f379cb8f-0007-5ac9-902d-2cd2c272b3ab","0ea467f8-17b2-5892-a179-75ee765ff795","fbf16cc2-9925-5178-9043-6ada4971a5ed","daa4b46f-aadd-5b27-8bc4-8b0a8446bf01","796004a6-8edc-5779-98bd-797d6b63914e","8c9c1271-5046-5a19-87aa-89640246b944"]}]}],"textures":[{"path":"ramp_stone_1.png","name":"ramp_stone_1.png","folder":"","namespace":"","id":"0","width":64,"height":64,"uv_width":64,"uv_height":64,"particle":false,"use_as_default":true,"layers_enabled":false,"sync_to_project":"","render_mode":"default","render_sides":"auto","frame_time":1,"frame_order_type":"loop","frame_order":"","frame_interpolate":false,"visible":true,"internal":true,"saved":true,"uuid":"57393f8e-8dee-5830-99ae-e9c5935c6ecf","relative_path":"ramp_stone_1.png","source":"data:image/png;base64,"}],"animations":[],"description":"# ramp_stone_1\n\nStone ramp, 1-step: one column wide, 1 column long (along +Z, climbing toward +Z), rising 4 u (1 terrain step of 11.25 cm).\n\n- Footprint: 1 x 1 columns (16 x 16 units, 0.45 x 0.45 m), centred on the origin, front (door side) faces -Z.\n- Finished bounds: x -8..8, y -2..4, z -8..8 units.\n- Texture: 64 x 64, 1 px per unit, square pixels, nearest filtering. Every visible face has its own texture region painted with its material at world position (seams line up across faces); identical faces share a region; construction and ruined pieces map into the region of the face they were cut from. No cube is cut to fit the texture.\n- Cubes: finished 4, construction_0 7, construction_33 7, construction_66 4, ruined 14 (8 rotated: roof slabs and a few leaning props).\n\n## Hit box\n\n- ramp wedge: 16 x 4 x 16 (walkable slope 14.0 degrees), centred at the origin\n\n## State group sets (children of `root`; show exactly one)\n\n- `finished`: the finished building (visible by default).\n- `construction_0`, `construction_33`, `construction_66`: build progress at 0 %, 33 % and 66 % (staked outline and scaffold, then walls rising inside scaffold, then full frame with roof rafters).\n- `ruined`: collapsed shell, broken walls, rubble, fallen roof (use with `_damaged.png`, or `_abandoned.png` for F7 abandoned buildings).\n- `ramp_stone_1_damaged.png`: damaged texture (scorch, holes, cracks) for the same UVs; works on every group set.\n- `ramp_stone_1_abandoned.png`: abandoned look (damage plus moss, faded cloth, cold fires) = `abandoned_ramp_stone_1` together with the `ruined` set or the finished set.\n"}